      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{66ab05b24e9acb1a90532e3a|full_name} The avatar you've created has some serious performance problems and may very plausibly be the cause of your performance suffering as a result. The avatar has too many:\n\n- visible material slots (31, Poor - max rendered logged as 115, Very Poor - recommended 4, good up to 8)\n\n- triangles (216,533 - VeryPoor - recommended < 32,000, good up to 70,000)\n\n- Skinned Mesh Renderers (22 - Very Poor - recommended 1, good up to 2)\n\n- animators (12 - Medium) for some forbidden reason (usually only need 1)\n\n- bones (332 - Very Poor - recommended max 75, good up to 150)\n\nParticularly, I suspect the excessive Skinned Mesh Renderers and material slots are the greatest contributor to CPU load and extra draw calls in these logs and a cause of problems (and not an issue attributed to the VRChat app).\n\nPlease try wearing an optimized avatar. Atlas your materials, merge your skinned mesh renderers, remove what you don't need/retopology.",
